---
args: {"desk": "PublicationDesk", "state": "ClaimReleaseState | null"}
returns: "ClaimReleasePacket"
---
1. Bind prior = state when supplied, otherwise an empty ClaimReleaseState at revision zero, bundleId desk.releaseId, and empty claims, candidates, reviews, receipts, revokedLineage and repairQueue. Bind claims = recoverQualifiedPropositions(desk). Keep source denials as opaque lineage events; remove their unsupported derived claims from releasable neighborhoods without naming the denied source to this reader.
2. Bind comparisons = compareClaimNeighborhoods(claims, desk). Only genuine overlapping-scope contradictions require authority arbitration. Bind authorities = resolvePublicationAuthority(comparisons, claims, desk.publicationHierarchy) for those contradictions; equal or missing authority blocks only the affected keys.
3. If no resolved contradiction or supported stale current-guidance link needs an edit, bind nextState: ClaimReleaseState = { revision: advance only if newly recovered claim identities or denied-source lineage changed the state; otherwise preserve prior.revision, bundleId: desk.releaseId, claims: append unseen source-and-edition claim identities while retaining prior claim history, candidates: prior.candidates, reviews: prior.reviews, receipts: prior.receipts, revokedLineage: append opaque new denial tokens to prior.revokedLineage, repairQueue: prior.repairQueue }. Return { state: nextState, comparisons, authorities, patchDrafts: [], releasablePageIds: prior.reviews with exact approvedBytes and no blockers, blockedNeighborhoods: unresolved or equal-authority comparisons, pendingSourceRequests: current unresolved source requests }. This no-edit result preserves existing state and does not manufacture a patch. Otherwise bind drafts = draftCoordinatedEdits(claims, comparisons, authorities, desk). Missing full current page text is a source request, never permission to invent an anchor.
4. For each draft and its exact readable page bind candidate = stagePageCandidate(page, draft). Collect candidates; any exact edit error blocks that page. Bind reviews = verifyStagedMeaning(claims, candidates, desk). Use actual re-extracted claims and protected meanings; a successful string edit alone does not establish fidelity.
5. Bind approvals = bindPageReleaseApprovals(candidates, reviews, desk). Only pages with current exact text approvals, resolved semantic checks and matching source versions enter releasablePageIds. Bind nextState: ClaimReleaseState = { revision: advance once for this new candidate/review state, bundleId: desk.releaseId, claims: append unseen source-and-edition claim identities while retaining prior claim history, candidates: append candidates by pageId and baseHash without overwriting prior candidates, reviews: append the new verification and exact approval results while retaining prior review history, receipts: prior.receipts unchanged because no publication receipt was supplied, revokedLineage: append opaque new denial tokens to prior.revokedLineage, repairQueue: preserve prior requests and append current page-specific patch, source and semantic blockers }. A concurrent base change requires re-reading affected anchors and renewed approval for changed meaning. Return { state: nextState, comparisons, authorities, patchDrafts: drafts, releasablePageIds, blockedNeighborhoods: page and proposition keys still blocked by authority, source or semantic checks, pendingSourceRequests: exact unresolved page-text or evidence requests }. No draft or approval binding is a publish receipt.
